WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.729
Punctuation Traps: When NOT to Punctuate

00:00:04.109 --> 00:00:06.495
No rule? No punctuation.

00:00:07.695 --> 00:00:08.693
How to spot it

00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:11.077
One choice with no punctuation

00:00:11.627 --> 00:00:13.530
A long subject before the verb

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.938
It’s testing: resisting punctuation that isn’t needed

00:00:19.138 --> 00:00:19.933
The method

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:22.406
Step 1: Name the parts

00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:24.653
Subject, verb, object?

00:00:25.203 --> 00:00:27.565
Step 2: Do they belong together?

00:00:27.845 --> 00:00:31.409
Subject–verb, verb–object: no mark.

00:00:31.959 --> 00:00:33.934
Step 3: Name the rule

00:00:34.214 --> 00:00:36.420
Can’t name one? Cut the mark.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.080
In a few words

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.615
No rule? No punctuation.

00:00:41.815 --> 00:00:42.638
The rules

00:00:43.038 --> 00:00:44.992
Nothing between subject and verb

00:00:45.272 --> 00:00:48.024
Wrong: The results of the study, showed…

00:00:48.304 --> 00:00:50.799
Right: The results of the study showed…

00:00:51.349 --> 00:00:52.658
Nothing before “that”

00:00:52.938 --> 00:00:55.383
Wrong: Researchers found, that…

00:00:55.663 --> 00:00:57.696
Right: Researchers found that…

00:00:58.246 --> 00:00:59.770
Nothing after “such as”

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.844
Wrong: such as: oak and maple

00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:05.203
Right: such as oak and maple

00:01:05.753 --> 00:01:08.273
Lists of three: commas between

00:01:08.553 --> 00:01:11.215
Right: ropes, tents, and food

00:01:11.765 --> 00:01:13.971
Blended quotes: no comma

00:01:14.251 --> 00:01:16.503
Wrong: called it, “a triumph”

00:01:16.783 --> 00:01:18.606
Right: called it “a triumph”

00:01:19.806 --> 00:01:20.846
Let’s try one

00:01:21.246 --> 00:01:27.317
The researchers who spent three winters tracking the migration of snow geese across the Canadian

00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:30.627
Arctic ______ that the birds’ routes had shifted east.

00:01:31.277 --> 00:01:33.559
This whole chunk is one long subject.

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:39.687
Then the verb, concluded, then what they concluded. These parts belong together.

00:01:40.237 --> 00:01:43.095
So no punctuation anywhere. Choice A.

00:01:44.295 --> 00:01:45.291
Common traps

00:01:45.691 --> 00:01:46.693
The breath comma

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:50.201
A long subject makes you want to pause. Don’t.

00:01:50.751 --> 00:01:52.228
Colon after “including”

00:01:52.508 --> 00:01:53.152
Never.

00:01:54.352 --> 00:01:57.481
Punctuation Traps: When NOT to Punctuate

00:01:57.761 --> 00:02:00.147
No rule? No punctuation.

00:02:00.697 --> 00:02:01.469
Spot it

00:02:01.669 --> 00:02:05.153
One choice has no punctuation; long subject

00:02:05.703 --> 00:02:06.410
Steps

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.719
1. Name the parts: subject, verb, object

00:02:10.999 --> 00:02:13.997
2. Belong together? → no mark

00:02:14.277 --> 00:02:17.520
3. Can’t name a rule? → cut the mark

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:18.823
Remember

00:02:19.023 --> 00:02:20.978
Nothing between subject and verb

00:02:21.258 --> 00:02:22.566
Nothing before “that”

00:02:22.846 --> 00:02:25.157
Nothing after “such as” / “including”

00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:27.518
Blended quote: no comma

00:02:28.068 --> 00:02:28.673
Trap

00:02:28.873 --> 00:02:31.067
The breath comma after a long subject

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:35.512
